      "writtenOn": "2019-09-17T00:24:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In my setup (Hatch \u003c---\u003e emark cable \u003c---\u003e Pixel 2) it was an SOP DiscIdentity request which was sent to the UFP (and the UFP responded with a NAK). In the current master, the PD message passing just stops after the NAK. With this CL, it\u0027ll try the SOP\u0027 DiscIdentity message to the cable.\n\nBut I imagine if there is any VDM NAK, we should still be able to probe the Cable characteristics.",
